//! C FFI bindings for the Obrain graph database.
//!
//! This crate exposes a C-compatible API that can be consumed by any language
//! with C interop support (Go via CGO, C# via P/Invoke, Dart via `dart:ffi`,
//! Ruby via FFI, Java via JNI, etc.). The surface of this crate is the C ABI
//! declared in `obrain.h` (generated by cbindgen), not a Rust API: the Rust
//! modules are private on purpose.
//!
//! # Memory Management
//!
//! All opaque pointers returned by `obrain_*` functions must be freed by their
//! corresponding `obrain_free_*` function. Strings returned by the API are owned
//! by the Rust side and must be freed with `obrain_free_string`. The full
//! contract (who frees what) is in `README.md`.
//!
//! # Error Handling
//!
//! Functions return `ObrainStatus` codes (or a null pointer). On error, call
//! `obrain_last_error` to retrieve a human-readable message. The error is
//! thread-local and valid until the next FFI call on the same thread.
//!
//! # Thread Safety
//!
//! An `ObrainDatabase` handle can be shared across threads. Internally it uses
//! `Arc<RwLock<ObrainDB>>` for safe concurrent access.
//!
//! # Access modes (décision D4)
//!
//! `obrain_open` opens READ-ONLY; writing requires the explicit
//! `obrain_open_write`, which holds the process-wide write lease (« bail »)
//! kept by the `bail` module and documented in `README.md`.

#![allow(unsafe_code)]

